using System.Collections.Generic;

namespace Pagedraft.Api.Tests;

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// RealProsePassages - TWELVE VERBATIM EXCERPTS OF A REAL, TWICE-PROOFREAD HEBREW MANUSCRIPT.
//
// WHY THIS FILE EXISTS AT ALL, AND WHY THE TEXT IS EMBEDDED RATHER THAN READ FROM DISK.
// The manuscript these passages come from lives in the WORKSPACE docs directory, which is OUTSIDE
// every git repository in this workspace (the PageDraft root is not a repo; src/docs/ is tracked by
// nothing). A fixture that opened that .docx at runtime would pass on this machine and fail on every
// clone, and - worse - would pass VACUOUSLY on a clone if the loader returned an empty corpus, which
// is the exact shape that has already burned this corpus once (LoadProofreadGold returning
// Array.Empty on a missing file). The prose is therefore embedded here, in the test project, where it
// is versioned with the assertions that read it.
//
// WHY REAL PROSE INSTEAD OF MORE AUTHORED FIXTURES. This corpus already has authored chunked fixtures
// (ChunkedAgreementFixtures) and their over-correction column is a PROXY: it counts every suggestion
// that is not the seeded agreement fix, which is only a precision measure if the authored prose is
// otherwise clean. This manuscript was proofread TWICE by a human before it was handed over, so on
// its text nearly every edit a model proposes is by construction an over-correction. That makes the
// metric a COUNT rather than a classification, and it removes the dependence on the phenomenon
// classifier entirely - which matters, because that classifier was audited on 2026-08-05 and found
// degenerate on this task (it emits only "agreement-repair" and "other").
//
// PROVENANCE AND CLEARANCE. Source: "זיכרונות של מכשף - לאחר הגהה שנייה.docx", ~107,600 words,
// cleared for use as proofread test data. Every passage below is a CONTIGUOUS run of paragraphs taken
// from the middle of the document (paragraph indexes 989-4235 of 5,640, i.e. never the opening and
// never the ending), so that the chunker produces genuine [CONTEXT_BEFORE] overlaps rather than the
// degenerate first-chunk-only case. Paragraph indexes are recorded per passage in
// RealProsePrecisionFixtures so an excerpt can be located in the source document again.
//
// SELECTION IS PART OF THE EXPERIMENT, NOT A CONVENIENCE. The candidate pool was every ~345-430 word
// contiguous paragraph run in the middle 70% of the manuscript (1,904 windows after the hygiene
// filters below). The twelve kept were chosen to span a DIALOGUE-DENSITY GRADIENT - two with no quote
// character at all, up to two above forty - because the single largest population of candidate edits
// on this manuscript is its ASCII double quote (the house style of the book; the corpus's own gold
// case norm-3 treats ASCII -> gershayim as a correction). If every passage were dialogue-heavy, one
// construction could carry the entire result, which is exactly the failure that made the synthetic
// measurement hard to trust: four instances of ONE construction carried 62% of the over-corrections
// there. The narration-only passages are the control for that.
//
// HYGIENE FILTERS APPLIED TO EVERY PASSAGE (each one is also asserted, not just applied):
//   - no word on the deterministic ktiv-male list, so KtivMaleChecker adds no arm-invariant
//     suggestions to the count;
//   - no NO-BREAK SPACE (U+00A0). An NBSP -> space edit is whitespace-only on BOTH sides, so it would
//     land in the WhitespaceOnlySuggestions TRIPWIRE that a run is voided on - a false void;
//   - no digits, no Latin letters, no niqqud, no bidi control characters, no brackets or colons;
//   - no single-word paragraph that is a point-of-view marker (the manuscript uses bare character
//     names as scene headers), so every passage reads as continuous prose.
//
// THE TEXT IS VERBATIM. Paragraphs are stored one string per source paragraph and joined by
// RealProsePrecisionFixtures.ParagraphSeparator. Nothing is normalized here: the en-dashes, the
// maqafs, the ellipses, the geresh apostrophes and the ASCII quotes are the author's, and they are
// the edit candidates the measurement is about.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

/// <summary>The twelve excerpts, one <c>string[]</c> of paragraphs each. See the file header.</summary>
public static class RealProsePassages
{
